// The Java binding's classes, compiled once and shared by the whole JVM
// family: kotlin/, groovy/ and clojure/ all layer over THESE classes rather
// than binding the engine a second time.
//
// Flat layout: the .java sources sit directly in this module dir (java/aether/),
// NOT under a Maven src/main/java tree. aeb's `java.javac` builder, with no
// source_layout set, globs *.java at the module root (depth 1) — which is
// exactly our layout. The sources keep their `package org.libphonenumber.ae;`
// declaration; javac reads the package from the file and emits the class tree
// under -d, so a flat source dir with a packaged class is fine (a Maven src
// tree is a build-tool convention, not a javac requirement).
//
// The important part is what this node publishes: the standard
// `jvm_classpath_deps_including_transitive` artifact, which every JVM SDK
// builder reads through `bldr._build_dep_classpath(...)`. The kotlin/groovy/
// clojure layers dep this node for the classpath.
//
// JDK 22+ is required: the binding is FFM/Panama (java.lang.foreign), final in
// 22. `release` is deliberately NOT pinned below that.

import bldr
import java

aeb(cap) {
    bldr.build() {
        java.javac() {
            // no source_layout -> flat *.java glob at this module dir
        }
    }
}
